Script 2: Real-Time Filesystem Sentinel Daemon (inotify)

Question: How do you construct an event-driven daemon that continuously watches a directory for new file creations using kernel notification APIs (inotifywait) and automatically moves them to a staging path based on file extension?
Bash

WATCH_DIR="/tmp/watch_input"
TARGET_DIR="/tmp/watch_output"

mkdir -p "$WATCH_DIR" "$TARGET_DIR"

echo "Monitoring $WATCH_DIR for incoming file events..."

inotifywait -m -e create -e moved_to --format '%w%f' "$WATCH_DIR" | while read -r FILEPATH; do
    if [[ "$FILEPATH" == *.pdf ]]; then
        echo "[EVENT] PDF Detected: $FILEPATH"
        mv "$FILEPATH" "$TARGET_DIR/"
    fi
done

#The Problem: Build an event-driven directory watcher for /tmp/raw_uploads. 
#Whenever a new .png or .jpg image is created or moved into the directory, extract the filename, output "[INGEST] Processing <filename>", 
#and move the file into /tmp/media_library/.

#!/bin/bash
set -euo pipefail

WATCH_DIRECTORY="/tmp/raw_uploads"
TARGET_DIRECTORY="/tmp/media_library"

mkdir -p "$WATCH_DIRECTORY" "$TARGET_DIRECTORY"

inotifywait -m -e create -e moved_to --format "%w%f" "$WATCH_DIRECTORY" | while read -r FILENAME; do
    echo "[INGEST] Processing "$FILENAME"
    mv "$FILENAME" "$TARGET_DIRECTORY"
done